title The rule spelled twice where routing is forbidden, and the cure that did not reach the hand
prompt Baton lap as COPAL -- take the next agent-doable lap in the amphora lane, Lindy-first crux-first.
rota lap 4234, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; its dual seat is the marked value, which is Amphora's own page, so the lap took the shoulder-line vow to the module and counted its reading sites instead of trusting the comment that counted them
think The earth row reads the concrete fact at the door before any argument. The marked value's dual seat names Amphora by image: the shoulder line says what rides inside. So I read amphora/manifest_entry.rye and counted rather than trusting.
think The contract's own comment justifies centralizing with a census -- all five reading sites -- and grep found six routing through parse_manifest_line: vessel_core:160, :167, and :234 in take_listed_line, which neither the comment nor the roster note names.
think Then the sharper find. amphora/src/main.rye:append_cargo_line reads the same three-field grammar through its own hand-rolled tokenizer and its own copy of the plain-bytes literal, and welcomes ONE root where the contract holds two. A manifest-marked cargo line passes six readers and dies there as CargoUnproven.
think It is unreachable from outside because that door writes what it reads: pour builds the cargo plain, seals it, restore opens the same plain. No vessel edit reaches it without breaking the AEAD seal, which is exactly why it stood since the module was written, and why amphora_mark_wreck -- seated the day before for this vow -- reads vessel-core's frame and never opens src/.
think Repaired where it lives. Added amphora/src/manifest_entry.rye as a symlink, the same bare-name idiom amphora/kumara.rye and tally_copy.rye already use, since Zig refuses an import escaping the root file's directory. The reader borrows me.mark_verdict and bounds the mark field with sp1 > me.max_mark_len ahead of it, so an over-long mark REFUSES rather than tripping mark_verdict's own precondition assert.
think A couples: marker on the mirrored literal was tried and refused -- amphora_bounds_agree compares a bound's spelled numeric value and answered marker_on_derived, which is the right refusal and pointed at the better home. A comptime assert against me.mark_plain_bytes is checked every build rather than when a guard runs.
obs Three legs added to amphora_mark_wreck, each proven to BITE: the elder narrower rule restored in a source pen, the bound line deleted, and a divergent literal planted whose build refusal is asserted to NAME the comptime tie rather than merely to be non-zero.
obs I fired REDS %569 a fifth time. To stop my own cold roster pass -- which I had wrongly left running while I edited, so it was going to answer tree_moved regardless -- I typed pkill -f standing_equipment_run. My shell exited 144, that row's exact signature; one peer --hot at 1,418s survives and the rest is unattributable.
obs The cure already existed: tools/f/fleet_call.sh bounds by /proc/<pid>/cwd, carries a witness, and process_reach is rostered. Every one of those reads TRACKED SOURCES, and a command typed at a session prompt is in no file -- which %569 wrote in its own third field. Repaired on tools/f/fleet_baton.txt and .claude/rules/the-baton.md, which reach every ship next lap with no per-seat edit. No new guard, and that is the finding.
obs The cold roster open was abandoned rather than believed: it opened before my edits and would have answered tree_moved. The reading that stands is the --hot pass after git add, which measures the tree this commit ships.
